{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"fish_trout","model_identifier":"fish_trout","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# fish_trout\n\nTrout (B8), 35 cm (12.5 u). Heartland streams.\n\nOlive back with a pink side stripe and dark speckles, pale belly, adipose fin. Rig: root > body (front segment) > body_mid > body_rear > tail_fin for the side-to-side swim wave; body > head > jaw; pectoral fins fin_r / fin_l.\n\n- Cubes: 15 (all unrotated unless noted). Texture 64x64, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Rest bounds (body, no held items): x -1.5..1.5, y 0.0..3.8, z -6.2..6.2 (faces -Z).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 1.8 x 3.0 x 12.5 (w x h x d) centred on x = 0, z = 0, from y = 0 (belly)\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `swim` | 0.7 | loop | body wave travelling to the tail (loop, played in place) |\n| `idle` | 2.4 | loop | gentle hover: slow wave, fins sculling, gills/jaw pulse (loop) |\n| `dart` | 0.3 | loop | fast flee, big tail beats, fins tucked (loop) |\n| `flop` | 1.2 | loop | caught, on land: lies on its right side and slaps up and down (loop) |\n| `death` | 2 | hold | rolls belly-up and holds; rests on y = 0 (the game can float it at the water surface) |\n\n## Move speeds (in-place cycles; stride matched to these)\n\n- `swim`: 17.8 u/s (0.5 m/s), wave cycle 0.7 s\n- `dart`: 88.9 u/s (2.5 m/s), wave cycle 0.3 s\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups, pivot in model units)\n\n\n## Variant textures (same UV layout)\n\n- `fish_trout_young.png`: young fish texture (use at half scale): paler, softer markings\n\n## Notes\n\n- Fish rest with the lowest fin on y = 0 so the same model lies correctly on land; in water the game sets the depth.\n"},"description":"# fish_trout\n\nTrout (B8), 35 cm (12.5 u). Heartland streams.\n\nOlive back with a pink side stripe and dark speckles, pale belly, adipose fin. Rig: root > body (front segment) > body_mid > body_rear > tail_fin for the side-to-side swim wave; body > head > jaw; pectoral fins fin_r / fin_l.\n\n- Cubes: 15 (all unrotated unless noted). Texture 64x64, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Rest bounds (body, no held items): x -1.5..1.5, y 0.0..3.8, z -6.2..6.2 (faces -Z).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 1.8 x 3.0 x 12.5 (w x h x d) centred on x = 0, z = 0, from y = 0 (belly)\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `swim` | 0.7 | loop | body wave travelling to the tail (loop, played in place) |\n| `idle` | 2.4 | loop | gentle hover: slow wave, fins sculling, gills/jaw pulse (loop) |\n| `dart` | 0.3 | loop | fast flee, big tail beats, fins tucked (loop) |\n| `flop` | 1.2 | loop | caught, on land: lies on its right side and slaps up and down (loop) |\n| `death` | 2 | hold | rolls belly-up and holds; rests on y = 0 (the game can float it at the water surface) |\n\n## Move speeds (in-place cycles; stride matched to these)\n\n- `swim`: 17.8 u/s (0.5 m/s), wave cycle 0.7 s\n- `dart`: 88.9 u/s (2.5 m/s), wave cycle 0.3 s\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups, pivot in model units)\n\n\n## Variant textures (same UV layout)\n\n- `fish_trout_young.png`: young fish texture (use at half scale): paler, softer markings\n\n## Notes\n\n- Fish rest with the lowest fin on y = 0 so the same model lies correctly on land; in water the game sets the depth.\n","resolution":{"width":64,"height":64},"elements":[{"name":"head","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-0.75,0.25,-6.25],"to":[0.75,2.5,-3.75],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,1.5,-3.75],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[18,0,19.5,2.25],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[0,0,2.5,2.25],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[20,0,21.5,2.25],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[3,0,5.5,2.25],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[22,0,23.5,2.5],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[24,0,25.5,2.5],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":